 results:\n   - Click the checkbox at the top left to select the page.\n   - If there are more than one page, click the blue link that appears: “Select all conversations that match this search.”\n   - Click the Trash icon (Delete).\n3. To auto-remove future Uber messages:\n   - Click the down-arrow in the search box (or Settings → See all settings → Filters and Blocked Addresses → Create a new filter).\n   - In the “From” field put: uber\n   - Click “Create filter”.\n   - Check “Delete it” and check “Also apply filter to matching conversations”.\n   - Click “Create filter”.\n\nGmail (mobile app)\n1. Tap the search bar, enter: from:(uber) and run the search.\n2. Tap the avatar/checkmark to select messages; to delete many at once tap and hold the first, then select more, then Delete.\n(Note: mobile may not show “select all conversations” — use the web UI for large-volume deletions and to create a filter.)\n\nOther useful options\n- Unsubscribe: open one Uber promotional email and click its “unsubscribe” link (if present).\n- Block addresses: open a message → menu (three dots) → “Block [sender]”.\n- Change Uber account notification settings on Uber’s website/app to reduce emails.\n\nIf you want, I can:\n- Provide the exact search string/filter text to copy/paste.\n- Provide short instructions for another mail client (Outlook, Apple Mail).\nTell me which and I’ll give that immediately.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_071e965a5f1ef39e016a9a08bd58fc87d0867395c4bd3ee821","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"in_memory","reasoning":{"context":"current_turn","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","status":"completed","store":false,"temperature":1.0,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":